  "body": "Found while tracing #2005 on upstream/main cda3d5896. This is a source-trace finding.\n\nThe editor preview rebuilds body facets in state_tool_body::tool_body_preview. tool_body_view::preview creates a body with machine_default=false. tool_body_page::envelope returns its raw profile bands.\n\nCollision checks use tool_body::judged. For a machine-default holder, judged calls HolderProfile::floored with the parameter holder. The collision check and sim_tool_body::for_operation therefore retain the conservative parameter-cylinder floor. The editor does not show that floor explicitly. A default holder narrower or shorter than the parameter cylinder can appear smaller than the shape being checked.\n\nKeep the conservative collision rule. Show its effective bands in the editor, or visibly distinguish the draft body from the checked shape. An explicit holder must continue replacing the parameter cylinder.\n\nDone means: a UI test uses a machine-default body smaller than the parameter cylinder and pins the displayed checked envelope; an explicit-body control still replaces the cylinder. No collision or post behavior changes.\n\nRelated: #2005.\n",
